  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I’m Dr. ___. You were admitted tonight for abdominal discomfort and constipation. How are you feeling right now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, doctor. I’m a bit better since I got here, but my belly’s been really full and sore for about a week. I haven’t had a bowel movement in days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned in the ER that you were taking Miralax and Dulcolax recently but stopped. Why did you stop taking them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They didn’t seem to help much, and I thought maybe they were making me feel worse. So I just gave up on them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But constipation can really build up, especially with your history. We don’t want you straining too hard—it can affect your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My heart? I didn’t know that could happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Because of your past heart surgery and blockages, straining increases the stress on your heart. We noticed your troponin—a heart enzyme—was a little elevated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no—is that a heart attack?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, not at all. The levels were only slightly up, and your EKGs don’t show any damage. It’s likely what we call ‘demand ischemia’—your heart worked harder than usual, probably from straining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I was really pushing hard trying to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. So we’re going to help you avoid that. We’ve restarted your usual bowel medications—Colace, senna, MiraLax, and we’ll add lactulose and possibly an enema."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try them again. But will they really work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They do work, but they need to be taken regularly, even when you feel fine. Skipping them lets stool build up, and then it’s harder to pass."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess I didn’t realize that. I thought only when I was backed up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a common mistake. We’ll make sure you have a clear plan before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also did a chest X-ray tonight. It shows some old changes from your past surgeries and a bit of atelectasis—collapsed lung areas—common after being less active."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had breathing issues before. Is that related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. You have a history of asbestosis and recent pulmonary edema from your last admission. But tonight’s X-ray doesn’t show fluid in the lungs, so that’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. I was worried it came back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring it. Now, about your bladder—you have a Foley catheter, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had it for years because my bladder doesn’t empty on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got a urine culture, and it grew a resistant E. coli—same kind you had recently. But your urine analysis isn’t showing signs of infection now, and you don’t have fever or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So do I need antibiotics again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. Since you’re not symptomatic, treating it could lead to more resistance. We’ve informed your urologist and PCP. In the future, we may discuss a suprapubic catheter to reduce infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve never heard of that. Is it better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-06-22 23:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For some patients, yes—it can lower the risk of UTIs. We’ll talk more with your urologist later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-06-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s your belly today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-06-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still full, but the pain’s less. I haven’t gone yet, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-06-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray this morning. It shows stool and air-fluid levels, but no blockage. So it’s just severe constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-06-23 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-06-23 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a Fleet’s enema today and continue the oral meds. We want to get things moving safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-06-23 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do whatever helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-06-23 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you had a bowel movement after the enema. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-06-23 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better! My stomach feels flatter and the pressure’s gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-06-23 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly what we wanted. Your heart enzyme levels are also stable now, which is great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-06-23 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my heart’s okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-06-23 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. No heart attack. The strain likely caused the small rise, but now that you’ve passed stool, the stress is off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you this morning. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What should I do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take all your bowel meds daily—senna twice a day, MiraLax, Colace, and the others—even if you feel fine. Drink at least two bottles of water daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try to be more consistent this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, apply the miconazole powder to your scalp twice a day for a fungal infection we noticed. It’s mild."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I’ve had an itchy spot there. I didn’t think much of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This should clear it up. And keep all your follow-up appointments, especially with your urologist and PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re discharging you with home services for a little extra support. Call us if the pain comes back or you can’t pass stool."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve learned my lesson—no skipping meds!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best plan. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-06-24 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications now."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
